### Limitations

You may not use the Software for or in connection with, or make available to
any third party for or in connection with, a Competing Use. A Competing Use
means making the Software available to third parties in a manner that
substitutes for the Software, provides the same or substantially similar
functionality as the Software, allows third parties to avoid purchasing a
license to the Software, or is otherwise competitive with the Software.

Competing Uses include, without limitation, hosting or offering the Software
as a service, or embedding the Software or otherwise offering a modified
version of the Software into or with a product or service you provide to
third parties, where such product or service competes with a paid product
or service offered by the Licensor that uses or incorporates the Software.

You may make competing uses of the Software after the Change Date specified
below (see "Grant of Future License"). If your use of the Software does not
meet the definition of a Competing Use either currently or after the Change
Date, you are not subject to this restriction.

### Conditions

If you make any use of the Software, you must preserve, in the source code
of any derivative works you create as well as in any related documentation,
all copyright, patent, trademark, and attribution notices from the source
form of this Software that are provided to you.

If you distribute the Software, you must make the source form of the
Software available to any recipient (which may be satisfied by including
this License and a link to the Licensor's public source repository), and you
must license any derivative work you distribute under the same terms of this
